The '''2006 FIFA Club World Cup final''' took place at the [[International Stadium Yokohama]], Japan on 17 December 2006.

The match pitted [[Sport Club Internacional|Internacional]] of Brazil, the [[CONMEBOL]] club champions, against [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] of Spain, the [[UEFA]] club champions. Internacional won 1–0, after a counter-attack led by [[Iarley]] and the goal scored by [[Adriano Gabiru]] at the 82nd minute, in a match watched by 67,128 people. In doing so, Internacional won their first [[FIFA Club World Cup]]/[[Intercontinental Cup (1960–2004)|Intercontinental Cup]] and Barcelona remained without any world club title. [[Deco]] was named as [[man of the match]].<ref name="MoM">{{cite web|url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablest/toyotamvp.html |title=Toyota Cup – Most Valuable Player of the Match Award |access-date=2008-11-06 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081022190908/http://www.rsssf.com/tablest/toyotamvp.html |archive-date=22 October 2008 |url-status=live }}</ref>

